  "summary_of_theorems": {
    "T1_single_path_z3_coset_invariant": "For any sign schedule epsilon in {-1, +1}^k with net sign S(epsilon) = sum_l epsilon_l, every single-path sum V_epsilon(t) = (X, Y) satisfies X - Y == S(epsilon) (mod 3). Balanced even schedules (k=2m, S=0) annihilate the mod-3 obstruction for all m >= 1.",
    "T2_paired_difference_sign_invariance": "The paired path-difference distribution Delta_epsilon(t, u) = V_epsilon(t) - V_epsilon(u) is invariant across all 2^k sign schedules epsilon in {-1, +1}^k.",
    "T3_universal_one_third_nonunit_law": "Every paired difference satisfies 3 | (Delta_X - Delta_Y) over Z and (Delta_X, Delta_Y) == (sum_l epsilon_l (u_l - t_l)) * (1, 1) (mod 3), so exactly 9^k / 3 = 3^(2k-1) pairs have v_3(Delta) >= 1 and 2 * 3^(2k-1) have v_3(Delta) = 0 for all k >= 1."
  },
